hyprshutdown: exit 2 when the user cancels

hyprshutdown exits 0 whether every app closed, the user forced them closed or
the user pressed Cancel, so a caller that runs a reboot or power off after it
(with --no-exit) can't tell a cancel from a finish. Its log can't settle it
either: Cancel logs nothing, the last 150 ms check can already read zero apps,
and app classes are logged verbatim, so a class containing a newline can forge
log lines. Exit 2 on Cancel, and 1 when the UI backend fails to start (the
status was ignored before), so the outcome comes from something app text
can't touch.

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@
     // Capture VT switch option before running UI
     auto vtSwitch = parser.getInt("vt");
 
-    g_ui->run();
+    const bool RAN = g_ui->run();
 
     // VT switch for NVIDIA+SDDM: after Hyprland exits, the display may not
     // automatically switch back to the greeter's VT, causing a black screen.
@@ -103,5 +103,10 @@
         proc.runAsync();
     }
 
-    return 0;
+    // Exit 0 for every ending would make Cancel indistinguishable from apps closing; a
+    // caller deciding whether to go on and reboot needs a status app text can't forge.
+    if (!RAN)
+        return 1;
+
+    return g_ui->m_cancelled ? 2 : 0;
 }
diff --git a/src/ui/UI.cpp b/src/ui/UI.cpp
--- a/src/ui/UI.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/UI.cpp
@@ -208,6 +208,10 @@
 }
 
 void CUI::exit(bool closeHl) {
